    "workhouse master",
    "matron"
   ],
   "kind": "poor law",
   "meaning": "The institution where poor people were housed and set to work. A workhouse master and matron supervised its day-to-day running for the board of guardians.",
   "sources": [
    {
     "title": "The National Archives research guide: Poverty and the Poor Laws",
